  "35224769": {
    "cueTypes": [
      "electrolyte-review"
    ],
    "verification": "abstract-read",
    "safeflowSummary": "This updated Joint British Diabetes Societies guideline on adult diabetic ketoacidosis management highlights the high prevalence of hypoglycaemia and hypokalaemia seen with the previous protocol, and now recommends slowing the insulin infusion rate once glucose falls below 14 mmol/L. It also flags the newer risk of euglycaemic ketoacidosis in patients on SGLT2 inhibitors, a presentation that is easy to miss because blood glucose can look reassuring. SafeFlow's electrolyte-review cue points to this guideline because potassium and glucose trends in DKA management are a recurring source of harm that structured review can catch early."
  },
