  "41142216": {
    "cueTypes": [
      "deteriorating-obs",
      "score-comparison"
    ],
    "verification": "abstract-read",
    "safeflowSummary": "In a large Singapore validation cohort of nearly 59,000 ward admissions, NEWS2 discriminated overall clinical deterioration well (AUROC 0.90) and mortality especially strongly (AUROC 0.96), but its ability to flag unplanned ICU admission or code-blue activation was only moderate. Performance also varied across prediction windows from 4 to 72 hours, meaning the same score behaves differently depending on which outcome and time horizon a ward team is watching for. SafeFlow uses this as a reminder that a 'normal' trending NEWS2 score is not equally reassuring for every kind of deterioration."
  },
